WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.469
Winter came to an end, and Heidi and Grandfather moved back up the mountain at the first sign of spring.

2
00:00:07.470 --> 00:00:14.326
The snow had disappeared, and the mountain flowers were already showing their bright heads above the grass.

3
00:00:14.327 --> 00:00:18.297
Heidi was happy to be at home again.

4
00:00:18.301 --> 00:00:24.444
She danced with all the little beetles and winged insects that jumped and crawled in the sun.

5
00:00:24.445 --> 00:00:31.405
She imagined that the tiny creatures were as happy as she and that their chirping voices were singing,

6
00:00:31.406 --> 00:00:35.053
"On the mountain! On the mountain!"

7
00:00:35.054 --> 00:00:40.115
Late one spring afternoon, Peter arrived from his day up the mountain.

8
00:00:40.116 --> 00:00:47.237
He pushed his way through the goats to hand Heidi a letter, which he had forgotten to deliver that morning.

9
00:00:47.238 --> 00:00:50.240
When she saw it, Heidi was thrilled.

10
00:00:50.241 --> 00:00:55.272
"It's from Frankfurt, it's from Clara!" she said.

11
00:00:55.273 --> 00:00:58.553
She opened it and read it aloud.

12
00:00:58.554 --> 00:01:03.654
Clara was well enough to visit, and she and Grandmamma were on their way.

13
00:01:03.655 --> 00:01:07.128
"I can hardly wait," said Heidi.

14
00:01:07.129 --> 00:01:12.239
"Clara and Grandmamma! How much fun we will have!"

15
00:01:12.240 --> 00:01:14.969
Peter was not very convinced.

16
00:01:14.970 --> 00:01:19.596
Every time Heidi had a visitor, she spent less time with him.

17
00:01:19.597 --> 00:01:28.204
Peter suddenly jumped up and chased the goats at full speed down the mountain, but Heidi was too happy to notice Peter's mood.

18
00:01:28.205 --> 00:01:34.183
The days went by, and Heidi and Grandfather prepared their house for their guests.

19
00:01:34.184 --> 00:01:43.128
The sound of sawing and chopping came from behind the hut as Grandfather made chairs for their new visitors with his skillful hands.

20
00:01:43.129 --> 00:01:50.357
On a day that felt as if spring had finally turned to summer, Heidi looked down the mountain and cried,

21
00:01:50.358 --> 00:01:54.719
"Grandfather, Grandfather, come look!"

22
00:01:54.720 --> 00:01:58.555
A strange procession was making its way up the mountain.

23
00:01:58.556 --> 00:02:06.583
In front, two men carried between them a chair on poles, and in it sat a girl, very carefully wrapped up.

24
00:02:06.584 --> 00:02:15.345
A handsome woman followed, riding on a horse and looking with wonder at the surrounding mountainside.

25
00:02:15.346 --> 00:02:21.220
Finally, another man pushed an empty wheelchair, piled with a bundle of blankets.

26
00:02:21.221 --> 00:02:24.032
"Here they come, here they come!"

27
00:02:24.033 --> 00:02:26.837
shouted Heidi, jumping with joy.

28
00:02:26.838 --> 00:02:34.061
When the procession arrived, Heidi rushed forward, and the two girls embraced each other with delight.

29
00:02:34.062 --> 00:02:39.748
Grandmamma got down from her horse and gave Heidi an affectionate greeting as well.

30
00:02:39.749 --> 00:02:46.144
"What a magnificent residence you have, Grandfather," said Grandmamma.

31
00:02:46.179 --> 00:02:51.667
"I don't know which way to look first, it is all so beautiful.

32
00:02:51.668 --> 00:02:56.128
What do you say, Clara, what do you say?"

33
00:02:56.129 --> 00:02:59.344
Clara gazed around her with amazement.

34
00:02:59.345 --> 00:03:04.029
She had never imagined, much less seen, anything so splendid.

35
00:03:04.030 --> 00:03:09.210
"I can hardly believe how beautiful it all is," she said.

36
00:03:09.211 --> 00:03:18.116
They settled Clara into her wheelchair, and Heidi wheeled her around to show her the fir trees and the goats' shed.

37
00:03:18.117 --> 00:03:25.673
It wasn't easy to push the chair, but Heidi used all her might and managed to give Clara a full tour.

38
00:03:25.674 --> 00:03:34.946
"Oh, Heidi, if only I could walk, you could show me everything on the mountain," said Clara, a little sadly.

39
00:03:34.947 --> 00:03:43.729
While the girls were looking around and talking, Grandmamma and Grandfather got to know one another and set out the supper.

40
00:03:43.730 --> 00:03:52.779
Grandfather brought out the new chairs, and soon, they were all sitting down to a nice meal on the mountainside.

41
00:03:52.780 --> 00:04:02.101
After the meal, Grandfather appeared from the shed, carrying two bowls of goat's milk, one for Heidi and one for Clara.

42
00:04:02.102 --> 00:04:06.989
Clara had never tasted goat's milk before and found it delicious.

43
00:04:06.990 --> 00:04:13.504
"Tomorrow, we will drink two bowls," said Grandfather with satisfaction.

44
00:04:13.505 --> 00:04:17.643
The time passed happily, then Grandmamma said,

45
00:04:17.644 --> 00:04:20.997
"We must get ready to go, Clara.

46
00:04:20.998 --> 00:04:28.045
The sun is going down and the men will be here to carry you down to Dorfli soon."

47
00:04:28.046 --> 00:04:31.587
Clara looked up at the cloudless sky over the hut.

48
00:04:31.588 --> 00:04:40.341
"Oh, Grandmamma," she said, "I would like to stay here forever."

